    "form": "library",
    "maturity": "production",
    "analysis": "OpenDataLoader PDF is an open-source, benchmark-leading PDF parser (Java core with Python/Node.js/Java SDKs) that converts PDFs into Markdown, JSON with bounding boxes, HTML, and Tagged PDF/PDF-UA output, combining a fast deterministic local mode with an AI-backed hybrid mode for complex tables, OCR, formulas, and charts. It doubles as an accessibility-automation tool, auto-tagging untagged PDFs for screen readers (Apache 2.0) with enterprise PDF/UA export, built in collaboration with the PDF Association and veraPDF. It targets developers building RAG/LLM ingestion pipelines from PDFs as well as teams needing to meet PDF accessibility regulations (EAA, ADA, Section 508) at scale.",
